# Computational Thinking in Thinking Critically About AI

Throughout Thinking Critically About AI, students practice a set of problem-solving habits to investigate AI systems systematically. These habits are examples of **computational thinking**: an approach to understanding complex systems, identifying patterns, and making informed decisions.

Rather than teaching computational thinking as a separate topic, the unit embeds these practices directly into lessons.

## Computational Thinking Practices in the Unit

