## Instructional Focus
Teachers do not need to formally lecture on computational thinking vocabulary throughout the unit. Instead, the instructional goal is to help students practice these habits naturally through investigations, discussion, reflection, and revision.

When facilitating discussions, look for opportunities to ask questions like:

<div style="width: 80%; margin: 40px auto;">

<!-- Quote 1 -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 18px;">
  <img 
    src="https://images.code.org/4086844cf82c87eb1c9faf23d2d5f227-image-1744318038281.png" 
    alt="" 
    style="width: 70px; height: 70px; border-radius: 50%;">
    
  <div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; padding: 15px; font-size: 16px; max-width: 600px; border-radius: 10px;">
    “What pattern are you noticing?”
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Quote 2 -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 18px; flex-direction: row-reverse;">
